      "prognosis": "Course ranges from brief recurrent episodes to persistent symptoms. Some people recover fully, while others improve gradually or continue to have fluctuating detachment. Earlier recognition, reduced catastrophic interpretation, treatment of coexisting conditions, regular sleep, substance avoidance, and suitable psychotherapy may improve function, but there is no universal timeline or guaranteed response. Persistent symptoms do not mean loss of reality testing or deliberate behavior.",
