      "sourceNote": "Original ANI nursing synthesis. WHO and DSM support the intentional-falsification, presentation-as-ill, external-incentive, exclusion, and differential boundaries. MSD Manual provides secondary clinical support for identified deception, genuine-illness coexistence, nonconfrontational coordinated care, and limited treatment evidence. SAFE-T supports individualized suicide assessment and safety planning. No pattern clue is presented as diagnostic proof, and the card never authorizes withholding genuine care.",
