      "sourceNote": "Original ANI nursing synthesis. WHO and DSM support the perpetrator diagnosis, intentional-falsification, presentation-as-ill, external-incentive, and victim distinction. AAP, NICE CG89, NICE NG76, and APSAC support victim-centered terminology, genuine-illness coexistence, objective chronology, multidisciplinary safeguarding, reporting, and protection planning. Safeguarding guidance is applied within local law and policy; no clue is presented as proof, and perpetrator treatment never substitutes for victim protection.",
