      "sourceNote": "Original ANI nursing synthesis. WHO and DSM support individual psychotic-disorder assessment and medical, mood, substance, cognitive, and cultural differentials. APA's DSM-5 change summary documents removal of shared psychotic disorder as a separate diagnosis, and the DSM-5-TR clarification supports the individual other-specified relationship-context example without assuming a romantic partner or one source disorder. VA/DoD and NICE CG178 support comprehensive psychosis assessment and individualized treatment; VA communication guidance, NICE NG10, and SAFE-T support nonconfrontational communication, least-restrictive care, suicide assessment, and safety planning. No source makes separation or medication automatic.",
